 1. Connect via MySQL Workbench (easiest method)
 Step 1: Open Workbench

Launch:

MySQL Workbench
 Step 2: Create a connection

Click:
 “+” (New Connection)

Fill in:

Connection Name: Local MySQL
Hostname:  localhost
Port: 3306
Username: root
 Step 3: Save password

Click “Store in Vault…” (or “Save Password”)

Enter your MySQL root password.

 Step 4: Test connection

Click:
 “Test Connection”

If successful → ✔ “Successfully made the MySQL connection”

 Step 5: Open connection

Click the saved connection → it opens SQL editor.

 2. Connect via Command Line (CMD / Terminal)
 Step 1: Open terminal

Windows:

Command Prompt (CMD)
 Step 2: Login
mysql -u root -p
 Step 3: Enter password

Type your password (it won’t show while typing)

 If successful, you see:
mysql>

Now you're inside MySQL server.

 3. Verify connection

Inside MySQL run:

SHOW DATABASES;

or:

SELECT VERSION();
